{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style","id":64206,"title":"Lunar Hero Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-03T12:26:58-08:00","id":64206,"title":"Lunar Hero Style","content":"I know TDO has rewritten LHS before he was an author, but I can't find his rewrite, unfortunately. But in any case, unlike the other Hero Styles, I don't feel it really captures the Lunar Hero. Has anyone created a different Lunar Hero Style that not only works well, but showcases the Lunar Hero, and his/her unique approach to unarmed fighting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:30:25-08:00","id":64211,"title":"","content":"The Terrifying Argent Witches, a fan remake/reworking of the Lunars have a style.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpdom.com/resources/argent-witch-style.384/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpdom.com/resources/argent-witch-style.384/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpdom.com/resources/argent-witch-style.384/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.rpdom.com/resources/argent-witch-style.384/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:53:25-08:00","id":64235,"title":"","content":"I've rewritten it over ten times. The most recent is in the &quot;Lunar Fan Errata&quot; thread. However, over the year and a half since I reworked it, I've gone on board with the &quot;no Lunar Hero Style&quot; camp. White Reaper can then assume the same niche that Thousand Wounds Gear style does for Alchemicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:26:30-08:00","id":64270,"title":"","content":"Lunars are probably the only Exalt type that can truly get away with never needing anything but their native Charms when fighting unarmed. Some of the things from the core Lunar Hero style are really handy to have, but there's no reason you can't just drag that into the native charmset if you want.<br /> <br /> Why spend 90xp on a Charm series that nets you one ability and only works in conjunction with Martial Arts when you can spend 100xp and have all the enhancers for archery, firearms, thrown, martial arts, <b>and </b>melee?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T15:18:17-08:00","id":64339,"title":"","content":"Now that Hero Styles are gone as we knew them from 2e I think there will be no reason to separate the combat attribute charms into a dumbass &quot;brawlish&quot; MA. I do hope that the 3e Lunar book &quot;what night has bestowed&quot; or &quot;however they name it&quot;, solves the awkward relationship between lunars and MA's forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T15:19:59-08:00","id":64340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style?p=64339#post64339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that Hero Styles are gone as we knew them from 2e I think there will be no reason to separate the combat attribute charms into a dumbass &quot;brawlish&quot; MA. I do hope that the 3e Lunar book &quot;what night has bestowed&quot; or &quot;however they name it&quot;, solves the awkward relationship between lunars and MA's forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>By obviating the need and desire for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T16:02:43-08:00","id":64373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style?p=64340#post64340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By obviating the need and desire for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Errrr... no...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:25:49-08:00","id":64441,"title":"","content":"I hope to see Terrible Wolverine Onslaught return in some form.<br /> <br /> Overclocking yourself so much that you're tearing your body apart; using the regeneration Charms only allows you to remain even. Every turn, you ask yourself, &quot;Is the power worth the risk?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:35:14-08:00","id":64450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style?p=64441#post64441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope to see Terrible Wolverine Onslaught return in some form.<br /> <br /> Overclocking yourself so much that you're tearing your body apart; using the regeneration Charms only allows you to remain even. Every turn, you ask yourself, &quot;Is the power worth the risk?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at the end of a too-long stretch of Charms that have bizarre effects and prerequisites, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:54:30-08:00","id":64472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style?p=64450#post64450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at the end of a too-long stretch of Charms that have bizarre effects and prerequisites, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not.<br /> <br /> I assumed that would be merely understood. Because, yeah. Had enough of that shit two editions ago.<br /> <br /> On that subject, the original Coiled Cobra Strike might make for a good 3rd Edition Charm... as an entry-level trick rather than something at the end of bizarre bushes of unrelated Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T03:50:26-08:00","id":64733,"title":"","content":"<b>This is my version of the style:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FOOT-TRAPPING COUNTER<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 3m; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 3, Essence 1; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> One scene</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Combat does not end until the Lunar allows it. Against an opponent within hand-to-hand range, the Lunar's skilled footwork prevents that opponent from moving away from the character.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This counts as a reflexive </span></span></span><i>Blockade Movement</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> action, but it also works in order to prevent targets from fleeing. In order for an opponent to flee from the martial artist's great footwork (or try to get out of melee range), they need to make contesting rolls as for a </span></span></span><i>Blockade Movement</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> action, though the Lunar adds half his Dexterity, rounded up, in automatic successes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>RABID BEAST ATTITUDE<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 4m; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 3, Essence 2; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Foot-Trapping Counter</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The grace and speed of the Stewards is such that wounds, weights or weather cannot hinder them. The Lunar ignores all penalties to a Dexterity-based action in combat, including supernaturally induced penalties.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>THOUSAND CLAW INFLICTION<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 1m; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 3, Essence 2; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Reflexive (Step 1)</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> One action</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Foot-Trapping Counter</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Only the Lunar's skill limits him, not the restrictions of capability. The character's attacks each use his last attack position, defeating normal limits on the weapon. Activating this Charm allows the character to increase all Rate values to 5 if they are lower. Clinches get a Rate value equal to the number of limbs capable of grappling; a Lunar with two arms has Rate 2 and can simultaneously clinch two targets.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>LUNAR HERO FORM<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 5m; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 4, Essence 2; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Simple (Speed 5)</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Form-type</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> One scene</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Rabid Beast Attitude, Thousand Claw Infliction</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Drawing the Essence of Luna into him, the Exalt becomes an endlessly fluid warrior, seamlessly flowing from one movement to the next.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The character reduces Defense Value penalties from onslaught by 1 and from coordinated attacks by 2. He adds (Dexterity) to his Move and Jump ratings and his natural weapons become as powerful as a bull's, increasing minimum damage by 1.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If a Lunar is in </span></span></span><i>Deadly Beastman Transformation</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, all Lunar Hero Style Charms have their mote cost reduced by one (to minimum one mote), excluding this one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ARMOR-RENDING CLAW FIST<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 4m, 1wp; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 4, Essence 2; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Lunar Hero Form</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">With a single swipe, the Lunar's attack moves so quickly that it tears through even steel armor as though it were paper.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This Charm supplements an attack. If the attack hits the target (it does not need to deal damage), the target's armor soak is reduced by an amount equal to the Lunar's Strength (this does not affect natural armor). This soak reduction is permanent for mundane armor (or until repaired) and scene-long for artifacts or magical armor (including charms that give external armor). If the soak value is reduced to 0, mundane armor is completely broken beyond repair, artifacts lose their soak but retain their other effects. Charms break.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CROUCHING TIGER STANCE<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 7m, 1wp; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 5, Essence 2; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Simple (Speed 3)</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK, Counterattack</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> One scene</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Armor-Rending Claw Fist</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">To strike a Lunar is to taunt a tiger. All attacks against him suffer a -1 external penalty. In addition, when the Lunar successfully dodges or parries any close combat attack, he may launch a counterattack against the attacker. This Charm can be activated reflexively if activated together with </span></span></span><i>Lunar Hero Form</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>DEN MOTHER METHOD<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 3m; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 4, Essence 2; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Until DVs refresh</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Lunar Hero Form</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When a companion of the Lunar is in danger, he runs to his friend's aid. This Charm allows the martial artist to make a reflexive Defend Other action to a target within the range of his Move rating. This is independent from the Lunar's own actions. He can only defend one specific target until his DVs refresh.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>RUNNING THROUGH THE HERD<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 5m, 1wp; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 5, Essence 3; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Reflexive (Step 2)</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Den Mother Method</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In a combination of leading the attack, fooling his attacker and quickly dodging out of the way, the Lunar redirects a close combat attack that would otherwise have missed or been blocked toward someone else. The Lunar must be aware of the attack, which must have another valid target within the range of a Move action. That attack then plays out as normal. An attack cannot be redirected back at the attacker.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TERRIBLE WOLVERINE ONSLAUGHT<br /> <br /> Cost:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> --; </span></span></span><b>Mins:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Dexterity 5, Essence 4; </span></span></span><b>Type:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <b>Keywords:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> None</span></span></span><br /> <b>Duration:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Crouching Tiger Stance, Running Through the Herd</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When the martial artist activates </span></span></span><i>Lunar Hero Form</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, he may choose to enter a state of bestial fury. Doing this increases the Move and Jump bonuses from the Form-type Charm to (Dexterity x 3) and his natural weapons do lethal damage and may parry ranged and lethal attacks without a stunt. If the martial artist is a Lunar, he may also benefit from Fury-OK Charms as if he were activating </span></span></span><i>Relentless Lunar Fury</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The drawback to this Charm is that in order to acquire these benefits, the Exalt must enter a state that works like an uncontrolled </span></span></span><i>Berserk Anger Limit Break</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (</span></span></span><b>Exalted</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, p. 105). This effect can be broken mid-scene by spending three points of temporary Willpower, but doing so also cancels </span></span></span><i>Lunar Hero Form</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T05:39:03-08:00","id":64764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style?p=64340#post64340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By obviating the need and desire for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>MA is still valuable to Lunars when they want to practice strange and 'external' powers, or when they want to study a formalized universal fighting style alongside of others.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Hero problem is that Lunars can already do everything a Lunar Hero style could grant them using their own charms -- there's not really enough of a thematic statement in saying &quot;I'm a Lunar using Lunar Hero&quot; vs &quot;I'm a Lunar using Dexterity and Strength charms.&quot; But playing a Lunar using Fire Dragon or Ebon Shadow style offers you thematic and mechanical options that your regular Lunar charms wouldn't.<br /> <br /> (There is one advantage to hero styles -- they can be taught to outsiders and practiced with them, in theory -- but in practice that just led to serious mechanical and balance issues. Of course, that's not a problem unique to Lunar Hero, but there was less need for it than there was for the Ability-based hero styles, so it was always kind of a solution searching for a problem.)<br /> <br /> That said, if you want a replacement / reworking for Lunar Hero, I think the way to go would be something like the Immaculate styles -- MA styles that work well with existing Lunar abilities. I'd probably want to make it thematically distinct from the basic Lunar charmset, though, since the Immaculate styles also have this thematic that they're a way for DBs to transcend their limitations, and any Lunar-focused MA style isn't going to really offer that (so it needs to offer something else instead.) Certainly there's a lot of room for an MA style or two that happens to be useful if you've, say, got wings or claws or can charge on four legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-04-2014, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T09:36:38-08:00","id":64923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/64206-lunar-hero-style?p=64764#post64764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(There is one advantage to hero styles -- they can be taught to outsiders and practiced with them, in theory -- but in practice that just led to serious mechanical and balance issues. Of course, that's not a problem unique to Lunar Hero, but there was less need for it than there was for the Ability-based hero styles, so it was always kind of a solution searching for a problem.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I initially mourned the loss of the Hero Styles when John first told me that they were being replaced by Brawl charms because I'd done things like the Renegade Abyssal making a statement by learning Solar Hero Style.<br /> <br /> However I came to realise that this was slightly silly because there's nothing distinctive enough about Solar Hero Style for other characters to acknowledge that she was fighting like a Solar. I realised that what I really wanted for her was a MA style that showed she'd rediscovered her connection to the sun, I wanted Arms of the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> It was much the same story for the other characters I'd done this with, though not all their replacement Martial Arts exist ...yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}